# Members and methods renamed in one run. The styles are chosen so the two
# rules cannot land on the same name -- see the ruleset -- and cpp_format now
# refuses the combinations that can, so this is the shape that gets to run.
#
# The member half is fine: this found and fixed a real defect in it, where one
# rule's veto cancelled another rule's dependent-token resolution because the
# sidecar records had no rule index, so a member's declaration was renamed and
# its dependent use left behind. googletest's MatcherBase VTable is the case.
#
# What remains is the method half, and it is not a near miss: 11044 errors.
# Renaming member functions misses every reference that carries an *unresolved
# overload set* rather than a resolved declaration. Two shapes dominate:
# a call inside a template whose arguments are dependent, so overload
# resolution is deferred and the callee is an UnresolvedMemberExpr rather than
# a MemberExpr -- gtest-matchers.h calls Init(impl) from a constructor
# template, and Init is renamed at its declaration but not at the call -- and a
# using-declaration naming a member of a dependent base, as in
# using FlatTuple::FlatTupleBase::Get. Both are node kinds the cross-TU
# dependent-token path does not visit; it covers x.member and Helper<T>::member
# only. Sample counts: Init 1108, Apply 419, CastImpl 314, Get 164.
#
# So this is a real gap in the method scope, not in the combination: the ruleset
# is sound and the member half of it is green. Promote when the unresolved-
# overload shapes are handled.
#
# NB: this file is sourced by bash, so values must not contain backticks or the
# dollar sign.
REPO=googletest
RULESET=member_trailing_method_snake
EXPECT=known_fail
EXPECT_FAIL_PHASE=rebuild
EXPECT_FAIL_REASON='Renaming member functions misses references that carry an unresolved overload set: a call with dependent arguments (UnresolvedMemberExpr, not MemberExpr) and a using-declaration naming a dependent base member. The declaration is renamed and those uses are left spelling the old name. Minimal shape: template <class T> struct B { template <class U> B(U* p) { Init(p); } template <class M> void Init(M&& m); };'
